 \\\\ \\frac{10}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/bb/bb718fb5d9931c6f99268f40bbef401b50dc160304b271bd2035528bddabdec0.png) is an orthogonal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\dfrac 7 3,$ $c=\\dfrac{10}{3}$ and  \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{a}{c} = \\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac{7}{3}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{10}{3}\\right)} = -\\dfrac{7}{10}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133603 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5582" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133603 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the subspace $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ and an orthogonal basis $\\mathcal B$ of $\\textrm{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $\\mathcal B$ are given below. Given that $\\mathcal B$ is derived from $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\dfrac{c}{a}?$\n\n![](images/9a/9af89cb1c6f57895919cfec30701a6aa0da76adafcae91a0636b1e7ee3a89e1a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133603 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47fadc87-f265-5f1c-827a-28e5be9e8121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133603 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n![](images/fc/fc5495a909acfddca53e63d336f5d7c2261ee6df626f9db2ab9fe4f9714a3198.png)\n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n- **Step 1**: We set ![](images/8d/8db4c83e14f998397313580b16662b9c80e44bda34da21e8bf92b4a4e1d89ab8.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Next, we find $\\mathbf{v}_2$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for $\\mathbf v_2$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-5)\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/06/061b35426271be433b6f2a92dd3e189edfd3a725dd0fac17cb865a4984c0911d.png) is an orthogonal basis for $\\textrm{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=-4,$ $c=-1,$ and  \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{c}{a} = \\dfrac{-1}{-4} = \\dfrac{1}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133604 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5583" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133604 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the subspace $V$ and an **orthonormal** basis $\\mathcal B$ of $V,$ given below. Given that $\\mathcal B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$\n'\n![](images/9c/9c34e0953d430b0a657c7a784e1929a874479e507a1fa1082ceff8d4f3db6340.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133604 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "60dbc829-01fc-5283-8741-68af483d5313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133604 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's denote\n\n![](images/07/07343af18e216ada95c688294d28b29fb1e87e34e7e3485b1bf742295fcd2a44.png)\n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n- **Step 1**: We set ![](images/7d/7d5937987c8cbcab12bbb0f1349e330d221163ec557e7ae2aecee98b3cad072c.png)\n\n- **Step 2**: Next, we find $\\mathbf{v}_2$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for $\\mathbf v_2$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{6\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ![](images/61/61267a1a5ef9c57217e148bccbbfa84095d5e838c968ba2cb626c6ef8baa4f58.png)\n\n- ![](images/fa/fa5773aa1c638263efeb922d8c605068e0ec30070b01ee89c2c902f1977c81b8.png)\n\nTherefore, ![](images/99/990c25b329f93c269df9291bf8d6521bd7ff7e474f46815f95749abfb843fe83.png) is an orthonormal basis for $V.$\n\nFinally, $a=\\dfrac{2}{3},$ $b=-\\dfrac1  3,$ $c=\\dfrac{2}{3},$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c| = \\left| \\dfrac{2}{3} \\right| + \\left|-\\dfrac{1}{3}\\right| + \\left| \\dfrac{2}{3} \\right| = \\dfrac 5 3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048893 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354523 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186414753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding an Orthogonal Basis For the Span of Two Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133793 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "16e43d27-ffaf-58ea-bb6e-664b70770003" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133794